<Layout title="About Aaron Russell | Russell Tech" description="Meet Aaron Russell, the founder and technical lead behind Russell Tech in Leeds, with 20 years of experience building apps, websites and business systems."><section class="page-hero shell"><span class="eyebrow">About Russell Tech</span><h1>Small agency.<br /><span class="gradient-text">Big on doing it well.</span></h1><p class="lead">Russell Tech is led by Aaron Russell: a developer and digital builder from Leeds, with 20 years of experience working with good people and businesses across the UK.</p></section><section class="section shell split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Aaron Russell</span><h2>Close to the work.<br /><span class="gradient-text">Easy to talk to.</span></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Russell Tech exists to make good digital work feel a bit less complicated. No unnecessary layers, no vague handoffs and no technology for technology’s sake.</p><p>Aaron works across apps, websites, CMS platforms, CRM systems, cloud infrastructure and testing, bringing practical advice and technical know-how together from the start.</p><p>Across more than ten sectors and lots of projects, the common thread has been simple: understand the problem, build the right thing and make sure it works properly.</p><a class="button primary" href="https://aaron-russell.co.uk" rel="me">Find out more about Aaron ↗</a></div></section><section class="section shell manifesto"><span class="eyebrow">A few things we believe</span><div class="grid three"><article class="card"><strong>Keep it clear</strong><p>People should quickly understand what a product does and where to go next.</p></article><article class="card"><strong>Build it properly</strong><p>Performance, accessibility, testing and maintainability are part of the job, not extras.</p></article><article class="card"><strong>Keep it human</strong><p>Good communication makes the work better. Simple as that.</p></article></div></section><section class="section shell process"><span class="eyebrow">What working together looks like</span><div class="grid three"><article class="card"><span class="process-number">01</span><h2>Start with the problem</h2><p>We listen to what you’re trying to achieve, where things are getting stuck and what a useful outcome looks like.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="process-number">02</span><h2>Build the right thing</h2><p>We recommend a sensible route, keep the work clear and stay close to the detail as the product takes shape.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="process-number">03</span><h2>Make it work properly</h2><p>Performance, accessibility, testing and maintainability stay part of the job from the start.</p></article></div></section></Layout>
<style>.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.split h2{margin-top:1.5rem}.prose p:first-child{font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--ink)}.manifesto .grid,.process .grid{margin-top:2rem}.manifesto .card,.process .card{padding:1.5rem}.manifesto strong{font-size:1.2rem}.manifesto p,.process p{font-size:.9rem;margin:.8rem 0 0}.process-number{color:var(--cyan);font:500 .74rem/1 var(--font-mono)}.process h2{margin:1.4rem 0 0;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.3rem)}@media(max-width:700px){.split{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1rem}}
